WEBVTT

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:04.640
Sis, go for it!

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.970
I can't win like this.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.890
Haru, do the next motion.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:23.680
Oh. Yah!

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:24.430
Haru?

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.560
What're you do--

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:27.930
What are you doing?

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:31.100
There's only one week left
until the Nationals.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.640
Sorry.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.270
Let's stay focused and practice!

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:37.970
Right. Everybody, get in position!

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.020
Yeah!

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:02.350
<i>I'll put an end to spending</i>
<i>my days so thoughtlessly</i>

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:06.430
<i>I'm dying to break free of this</i>

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:12.140
<i>Since I can never take that first step forward,</i>

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:16.220
<i>you always take my hand and pull me along</i>

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:22.060
<i>You've brought me to see</i>
<i>something completely new</i>

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.350
<i>My whole world is changing</i>

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.560
<i>With that first step</i>

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:30.720
<i>I felt transformed</i>

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:35.680
<i>I can go anywhere; it'll work</i>
<i>out so long as we're together</i>

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.270
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:38.890
<i>just as you are</i>

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:42.060
<i>At times you'll feel lost and scared,</i>

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:48.600
<i>but there are so many things you</i>
<i>won't know if you never give them a go</i>

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.220
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:55.100
<i>stretch out your hands until</i>
<i>you're almost touching the sky</i>

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:58.350
<i>We're not alone anymore</i>

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:03.470
<i>Together we'll fly into a new world</i>

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:16.520
What're you smilin' about?

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.560
Readin' a message from someone?

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.390
Oh, it's from Sakura.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:21.310
Sakura?!

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:23.180
She can't be your girlfriend!

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:24.850
Another Saku.

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:26.930
Lemme see!

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:33.140
"First of all, the flyers aren't turning in unison,
and it sucks. The dance moves don't look sharp at all.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:35.680
Lastly, everyone has dead expressions."

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:43.310
Sakura is an old teammate from high school. We send
her the practice videos, and she critiques them.

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:44.810
So he's a huge masochist?

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:46.390
He really is.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.270
I'm glad for Sho.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.270
Yeah.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:54.060
He was able to talk to her properly.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:57.600
I said I'm fine, already!

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:01.470
No, you're going to the hospital
on the way home. I'll go with you.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.770
Takumi, are you feeling sick?

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:07.220
Come to think of it, it seemed
like you were coughing earlier.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:10.140
Nah, it's nothing serious,
but my brother here...

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:14.180
Takumi was sickly as a kid, so I'm worried.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:18.600
You worry way too much.
I'm going home without you today.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:26.890
A man is a man because he stands on his own.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:31.560
So the one who needs to do that is me.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.890
We've been together all the way
from elementary school to college,

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:39.100
but that won't be true in the future. And yet...

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.060
It's sad to let him go.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:48.850
When I quit judo, I wonder if maybe...

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:52.430
...Sis was sad, too.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.220
Is that your sister, Haru?

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:06.220
It really is. She's working hard.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.520
Haru, you go run with her.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.470
But we have to go to work.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:17.430
Say Haru will just be a bit late.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:18.770
Go on.

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:26.680
S-Sis!

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:34.140
What's wrong?

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:39.220
Uh, well... No, I mean...

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:40.970
What?

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:44.020
See, the thing is I--

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:44.970
You heard?

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:46.600
Huh?

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.180
That I can't win?

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:55.470
You're participating in the National
Cheerleading Championship, right?

00:04:55.470 --> 00:05:01.220
You've got to focus on that.
You don't need to worry about me.

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:02.640
Sis!

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:14.890
You've been wiping that cup non-stop.

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:17.060
Huh? Oh.

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:18.470
Haru.

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:21.220
If something's wrong, I'll lend you an ear.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:26.100
I'm not confident that I can give advice
as well as you or Kazu, though.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.100
Yeah.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.890
I'm here for you.

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:32.310
T-Thank you.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.560
Come on i--

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:34.470
Oh!

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:35.930
Hello!

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:42.020
I'll go clean the bathrooms.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:44.270
Huh?

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:47.600
Haru, congrats on both of us
passing the qualifiers.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:50.020
Y-Yeah. Hm?

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:53.350
Oh, I crashed again.

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:57.560
Here you go.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.640
I'm looking forward to this!

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:08.810
Yeah, I just knew this place had good
chocolate cake! Don't you think so, too?

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:10.850
Uh, yeah.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:12.470
Hey!

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.020
Tell me the recipe!

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:20.470
Well, my boss is out right now...
I'll ask when he comes back.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:23.310
Ah, then can you text it to me later?

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:25.020
Oh, sure.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:32.220
Sorry to put you through the trouble. It's almost
Valentine's Day, so I wanted to try making some myself.

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:34.430
If it turns out well, I'll bring you some!

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:35.600
What?!

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:46.680
Well, I get why you can't focus now,

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:49.810
but please don't make a bunch of
mistakes like you did at the qualifiers.

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:52.810
No, uh, that was different!

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:53.640
Mornin'!

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:54.850
Morning!

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:56.310
Oh, morning.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:58.020
You're early.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:00.640
I had a bit of a fight with my brother.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:04.720
I thought I could use some more practice.

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:10.850
1, 2, down, up!

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:13.350
Use your whole body more!

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:18.970
Thank you very much.

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:23.770
Don't rush into this, Saku.
Work on visualizing yourself doing it.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:24.720
I will.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:28.720
There's no practice tomorrow,
but make sure you train on your own.

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:30.470
All right, you're dismissed!

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:33.850
Thank you very much!

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:37.220
Haru! I've got work,
so I'm heading out now.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.520
Okay.

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:45.310
Saku.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:50.020
Wanna practice at my place tomorrow?
Kin and Hisashi are coming, too.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.450
Bandou Gym

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:56.310
1, 2, down, up!

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:01.430
Whoa, you did it beautifully!

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:04.180
So you <i>can </i>do it, Saku!

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:05.770
What a clean turn.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:08.390
You did great.

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:13.020
But somehow I can't do it well when
we're practicing with everybody else.

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:22.310
I'm sorry I'm such a weakling.
I've always been a crybaby,

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:26.270
and people have often said that my
older sisters are more manly than me.

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:28.770
You have sisters, too?

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.470
That must be great!

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:31.810
Huh?

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:36.140
My sisters aren't nearly
as nice as your brother is.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:41.390
My brother worries about me way too much.

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:47.770
He's having a hard time finding work, so I want
him to worry more about himself. Otherwise...

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:52.520
...I'll get fed up with myself
if I keep making him worry.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:56.270
Really. So every family
has their own problems.

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:58.970
You have an older sister, too, right?

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.100
Yup.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:06.220
We did judo together for ages.
But she was always the stronger one.

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:07.640
I see.

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:11.970
In my family, my brother's
the more accomplished one, too.

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:13.520
Same with my sisters.

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:21.970
I'm kinda glad I came today. I'm here because it
would've been awkward to face my brother at home.

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:27.600
But when I remembered everyone has their
own problems, like Haru said, my heart felt lighter.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:31.850
Yeah. We're the Little Brothers Trio, aren't we?

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:38.600
Well, I think I'll head home soon.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:40.020
Oh, okay.

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:45.680
Now I sorta want to apologize to
my brother for telling him not to worry.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.180
Apologize?

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:49.810
Then we'll head out, too.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:51.470
Um, Haru...

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:53.430
Ah, you leaving, too?

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:54.890
Well...

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:57.850
If you don't mind, I'd like you to help me.

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:03.720
Valentine's Day?

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:06.270
But that's when girls
make chocolate for boys.

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:08.680
Why worry about the details?

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:09.720
Huh?

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:16.390
Since Kazu's the reason why I decided to try
cheerleading, I want to do something to thank him.

00:10:16.390 --> 00:10:18.020
So...

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:21.600
What kind of chocolate does he like?

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.890
He might like stuff with almonds in it.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:26.310
Really? In that case...

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:32.390
I'll glaze these with chocolate. Then I'll cover them
with cocoa and make chocolate-covered almonds.

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:37.470
Mom, what are you doing?
It reeks of chocolate in here.

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:42.640
Oh, you're Haru's sister! I'm Sakuma,
one of his cheerleading teammates.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:45.520
Uh, I'm Haruko.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:49.020
Sorry for bothering you.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:50.970
Uh...

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:52.390
Sis!

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:57.060
Um...

00:10:57.060 --> 00:10:59.310
What's been with you lately?

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:04.350
It's... I... I finally figured
out what I want to say.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:07.560
Now I sorta want to
apologize to my brother.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:09.600
I'm sorry!

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.180
Huh?

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:15.970
I've always wanted to apologize
for quitting judo without telling you.

00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:23.100
What's more, I didn't quit
because of my injury.

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:30.060
I was torn over whether
I should keep doing judo.

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:31.850
Ever since that time...

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:37.020
Sis! I heard you got beat by
an upperclassman. Are you okay?

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:40.310
I envy you, Haruki.

00:11:40.310 --> 00:11:43.060
I wish I was a man.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:45.890
I want to be stronger than anyone else!

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:55.850
"Why can't I be a woman and she a man?"
"Do I have that much passion?"

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:59.930
I thought that so many times.

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:05.720
Before long, I'd beaten you only in height...

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:11.140
...but when it came to matches,
I simply couldn't beat your results.

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:15.850
You mean I was always
pushing you too far?

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:18.470
Uh, no, that's not it.

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:24.890
I decided myself that, rather than do judo
because we had a dojo and I looked up to you,

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:28.390
I might have my own path.

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:34.470
I see. You've started down a path
that's different from mine.

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:35.770
Sis...

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:37.720
But...

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:40.350
For me, there's only judo.

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:57.970
I heard everything.

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:03.520
I'm sure your sister will
understand how you feel.

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:06.220
Though maybe not right now.

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:26.470
Saku! That was such a nice, sharp turn!

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:28.350
You did it just right!

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:30.930
Bro, Saku did it!

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:32.020
You sure did!

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:34.220
Be sure to do this during the real thing.

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:37.770
Yeah, I think I can!

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:40.310
I decided to start thinking I could.

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:44.770
Just like the coach said, I've also
tried visualizing myself doing it.

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:48.470
Thinking "I can" instead of "I can't"!

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:50.390
Perfect!

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:55.270
I never thought I'd hear such wonderful
words come from someone close to me,

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:58.680
instead of from the sayings of a stranger.

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:01.560
Sakuma, I'm very impressed.

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:03.850
Saku, you are a man.

00:14:03.850 --> 00:14:06.680
--That's right!
--A real man!

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:14.140
Here's a token of my friendship.

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:17.600
You're looking forward to it, Haru.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:18.470
Huh?

00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:21.850
Man, I want some homemade
chocolate cake, too.

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:24.140
D-Did you hear that from Sho?

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:27.270
I'll probably get zero this year.

00:14:27.270 --> 00:14:30.520
No, I think you could get one.

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:31.850
Huh?

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:34.020
Happy Valentine's!

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.720
Why Kazu?

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:45.060
Kazu, you probably don't remember,
but at the school festival, you helped me up.

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:52.850
O-Oh, did I?

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:57.350
Because of that, I saw your
performance, and now I'm here.

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:59.850
This is to show my thanks.

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:02.810
Then I'll gratefully accept it.

00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:05.970
I can't eat all of these,
so please have some.

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:07.470
You have leftovers?!

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:11.060
I love chocolate. Thanks a lot!

00:15:11.060 --> 00:15:13.430
I haven't even gotten
some courtesy chocolate.

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:15.520
I got one from my brother.

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:17.520
And I only got one from Takumi.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:20.060
What's with such pointless gift-gifting?

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:21.930
I got one from Kirari!

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:22.930
Oh, me, too!

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:24.140
Why you?!

00:15:24.140 --> 00:15:27.220
She sent it to thank me for shoppin' with her!

00:15:29.890 --> 00:15:32.560
Guys with girlfriends can breathe easy.

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:36.470
Why does Tono have a girlfriend? Why?

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:39.470
Oh, I haven't gotten mine yet.

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:42.310
But she said she'd make
chocolate cake this year.

00:15:42.310 --> 00:15:43.770
Chocolate cake?

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:47.640
Yeah, she said there's a restaurant
with really tasty chocolate cake,

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:50.390
and she asked them for the recipe.

00:15:50.390 --> 00:15:51.600
Wow.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:54.850
Is that what's in fashion now?

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.270
Oh!

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.430
Koji!

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:06.520
Oh, hi, Chi!

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.560
Ah, 'scuse me for a sec.

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:17.970
"Thank you, Haru!"

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:21.680
Ton's girlfriend is a Dreams girl?

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:24.060
No wonder he knew so much
about cheerleading.

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:25.930
She's mega cute!

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:27.390
H-Haru?

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:29.430
Haru, I'm sorry! My bad!

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:31.930
What are you apologizing for, Kazu?

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:33.390
Uh, well...

00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:35.850
S-Stay strong, Haru!

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:37.890
Sorry I'm late!

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:44.350
Here, this chocolate's for all of you!

00:16:57.680 --> 00:17:02.180
My Valentine's Day specialty:
curried noodles with a pork cutlet heart!

00:17:02.180 --> 00:17:05.270
Hey, when you eat this, the heart breaks.

00:17:05.270 --> 00:17:08.520
Heartbreak noodles!

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:14.180
Chihiro said she and Ton brought some
chocolate cake to your workplace.

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:17.390
Sho says he'll bring some
here when his shift's over.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:18.270
Fine then!

00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:19.930
It'll be beyond bitter!

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:24.020
We're all behind you. Cheer up, Haru!

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:25.100
Uh-huh.

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:30.270
Brief though it may have been, how I
envy your heart-pounding experience.

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:34.310
So who said those all-too-true words?

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:36.270
Wataru Mizoguchi.

00:17:36.270 --> 00:17:37.930
<i>You </i>did?!

00:17:37.930 --> 00:17:41.850
From now on, I'd like to
speak in my own words.

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:45.060
Rather than borrow the words of others.

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:50.930
Until now, I was a theoretical person
lacking in any kind of experience.

00:17:50.930 --> 00:17:54.970
But then I did cheerleading,
talked to all sorts of people...

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:59.720
...and I came to comprehend things
I hadn't understood, or been able to see.

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.430
Same here.

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:05.350
Before, I did baseball and
everythin' in order to win,

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:10.270
but for the first time, I've experienced
workin' as a team to achieve sumthin'.

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:15.140
I've certainly learned a whole
lot of things from cheerleading.

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:18.770
Me, too. Other people are different from me.

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:23.100
And I've learned that that's
both annoying and exciting.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.930
As for me...

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:30.390
I've found that doing something
seriously is hard, but it can be fun.

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:32.020
Ditto.

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:39.720
I now get that, in order to make someone
smile, first you have to smile yourself.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:43.680
You've all overcome so much.

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:46.810
I need to do that, too.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:50.060
All right! We'll find another nice girl!

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:52.430
If you do, introduce her to me!

00:18:52.430 --> 00:18:54.850
I wonder if Ton is on a date by now.

00:18:54.850 --> 00:19:00.430
How irritating! Shall we send him
a picture of our heartbreak noodles?

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:07.390
I'm really sorry. I got you
all excited for nothing.

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:11.520
Nah, I'll definitely beat you next Valentine's.

00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:15.100
While I'm apologizing, I'll tell you this.

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:20.890
I heard there's an inter-university
winter tournament tomorrow. For judo.

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:23.680
But we have practice tomorrow.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:28.680
Won't cheering on a real
match be practice enough?

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:38.270
Haru

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:38.270
Mizoguchi

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:38.270
Yes

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:38.270
Skipping practice today

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:44.280
Tokyo Student Judo Inter-University Winter Tournament

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:08.430
Sis, fight! You can do it!

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:10.930
Sis! You can beat her!

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:13.640
Go, fight, win!

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:18.310
Begin!

00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:20.720
Yeah! Attack, attack!

00:20:22.770 --> 00:20:26.720
Sis, gooo!

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:31.680
One point!

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:49.680
Were you able to cheer her on?

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:53.270
She won.

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:55.640
Oh, well done!

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:58.270
Seems like my voice reached her.

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:02.560
'Cause the Breakers' ace flyer
was cheering for her.

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:05.060
Kazu! Haru!

00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:09.390
It's late, but here are your Valentines.

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:13.810
Haruko, thank you!

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:16.290
<b>50% Off</b>

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:14.970
Haruko, thank you!

00:21:14.970 --> 00:21:17.060
Sis, what's this?

00:21:17.060 --> 00:21:19.310
You bought the cheap stuff!

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:22.720
Guys who only get chocolate
from their parents can't complain.

00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:25.140
This year I got one from my coach, too!

00:21:25.140 --> 00:21:27.850
That's not worth boasting about, Haru.

00:21:29.770 --> 00:21:33.770
Hey, it's been a while,
so let's do some judo.

00:21:49.270 --> 00:21:50.020
Next!

00:21:50.020 --> 00:21:51.470
Please go ahead!

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:54.350
Not enough!

00:21:56.180 --> 00:21:57.100
Do it again!

00:21:57.100 --> 00:21:58.270
Right!

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:06.100
Not bad, Haruko.

00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:08.430
Sis, you're amazing!

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:11.270
What about you guys?

00:22:11.270 --> 00:22:16.430
I'm going to watch the
Nationals, too. Do your best!

00:22:16.430 --> 00:22:18.060
Yeah.

00:22:18.970 --> 00:22:22.970
Bittersweet Valentine

00:22:32.850 --> 00:22:36.390
<i>Without even thinking, I shouted a reply</i>

00:22:36.390 --> 00:22:43.020
<i>The voice opening that new door</i>
<i>sounded like a tightly clenched fist</i>

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:46.430
<i>Resounding with reassuring determination</i>

00:22:46.430 --> 00:22:49.810
<i>I think if I let out</i>
<i>(I've been waiting for this)</i>

00:22:49.810 --> 00:22:53.100
<i>All my pent-up energy</i>
<i>(I can change something)</i>

00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:59.680
<i>We've always been looking for</i>
<i>something this cool! Ain't that right?</i>

00:22:59.680 --> 00:23:02.600
<i>Feeling insecure</i>
<i>(Oh my God!)</i>

00:23:02.600 --> 00:23:05.890
<i>I fell into a funk</i>
<i>(Oh my pride!)</i>

00:23:05.890 --> 00:23:07.970
<i>Send that old me</i>
<i>(Don't give in!)</i>

00:23:07.970 --> 00:23:09.640
<i>A solid cheer</i>
<i>(Go, go!)</i>

00:23:09.640 --> 00:23:14.140
<i>Make encouraging motions</i>
<i>(Let's dance together!)</i>

00:23:14.140 --> 00:23:17.520
<i>Yes! Fly high, fly dive, up and away!</i>

00:23:17.520 --> 00:23:21.270
<i>Never hang your head and give up</i>
<i>(No!) </i>

00:23:21.270 --> 00:23:24.600
<i>Break up, break out, break it to smithereens</i>
<i>(Yes!)</i>

00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:27.890
<i>Smile together, break a sweat, show your guts!</i>
<i>(Guts!)</i>

00:23:27.890 --> 00:23:34.520
<i>Strike a victory pose toward the blue sky</i>
<i>(Jump! Jump! High V!)</i>

00:23:34.520 --> 00:23:37.680
<i>Win over everybody's hearts!</i>

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:41.060
<i>Go for that moment when</i>
<i>you meet a sparkling smile</i>

00:23:44.390 --> 00:23:49.180
<i>Go, fight! Go, fight, win!</i>

00:23:54.140 --> 00:23:59.850
B-R-E-A-K-E-R-S! Go, Breakers!

00:23:59.850 --> 00:24:06.100
Let's go, Meishiin! Go for love and peace!

00:24:06.100 --> 00:24:10.970
Next Episode: Cheer Boys!

00:24:06.100 --> 00:24:06.350
Let's go, Meishiin! Go for love and peace!

00:24:06.350 --> 00:24:08.270
Next Episode: Cheer Boys!

00:24:08.270 --> 00:24:10.970
Let's go, Breakers!
